  "assumptions": "Illustrative whole-facility finite hydrogen stores, not pressure/kinetics/safety or vendor calibration. Liquid near20.27K para-rich hydrogen relative to25C normal gas has -1.24kWh/kg endpoint enthalpy including ortho/para conversion, separate from12kWh/kg liquefaction AC. Fixed0.1%/day boiloff is a teaching assumption; vent ends as25C normal gas and absorbs1.24kWh/kg ambient heat. Active discharge uses finite ambient vaporizer plus actual auxiliary AC. LaNi5 dry host is immutable and offers1.2%dry-mass usable hydrogen, binding enthalpy-4.275kWh/kgH2. Desorption process heat is cycle-average internal load, not an extra energy inventory. No external useful heat or cold-power output. Charge electricity renewable-only; active discharge auxiliaries can use wind/PV or finite electrical storage, never fuel-cell/turbine output.",
